AbstractNonsense/PullbackAddGrp.lean
------------------------------------
[ ] AddGrpObj (pullback f g)                                         (l.43)
      The pullback of two group homomorphisms f : G → T, g : H → T is
      again a group object (addition and zero taken componentwise).
      zero_add is started (two `have`s left as sorry).
      Still missing: zero_add, add_zero, add_assoc, neg, left_neg, right_neg.

[ ] IsCommAddMonObj (pullback f g)                                   (l.65)
      If G and H are commutative, so is their pullback.

[ ] IsAddMonHom (pullback.fst f g)                                   (l.71)
      The projection G ×_T H → G is a group homomorphism.

[ ] IsAddMonHom (pullback.snd f g)                                   (l.73)
      The projection G ×_T H → H is a group homomorphism.

[ ] IsAddMonHom.pullback_lift                                        (l.75)
      A map into the pullback built from two group homomorphisms is
      itself a group homomorphism.


