AbelianVarieties/TateModule.lean
--------------------------------
Points are now geometric points: morphisms from `gspec K` = Spec K̄ (with
K̄ = `AlgebraicClosure K`), instead of K-points from `specᵤ K`.

[x] torsion_map_comp
      Done (9dca10f): the scheme-level identity
        ker_int_hom (k ∣ n) = ker_int_hom (m ∣ n) ≫ ker_int_hom (k ∣ m)
      via pullback.hom_ext + int_hom_comp.

[-] int_hom_rational, rational_torsion                               (l.42–60)
      Commented out ("probably don't need this"). If needed after all,
      move to AbstractNonsense / IntHom. rational_torsion still lacks the
      inductive step and the final goal.

[ ] finite_torsion_points                                            (l.65)
      A[n](K̄) is finite when n ≠ 0.
      In progress (2b5817e): the proof now gets IsFinite A[n].hom, IsAffine
      A[n].left, Module.Finite Γ(Spec K, ⊤) Γ(A[n].left, ⊤), and that
      Γ(A[n].left, ⊤) is Artinian.
      Note: `have := hhom ▸ step₂ hn` needs the explicit type
      `IsFinite (A[n]).hom`, otherwise the hidden source/target stay as
      (pullback …).left / (𝟙_ _).left and instance search fails.
      Still missing:
        - Finite (Γ(A[n].left, ⊤) →ₐ[Γ(Spec K, ⊤)] Γ(Spec K, ⊤))   (l.89)
        - the final goal (l.92).
      These are still stated for K-points; they need changing to K̄-points
      (algebra maps into K̄, finitely many because the algebra is finite
      over K), probably using the base change functor.
      The old proof is kept in a comment below the sorry.

[ ] tate_module_representation                                       (l.271)
      A homomorphism f : A → B induces T_ p (A) → T_ p (B).
      functorial_ker_int (IntHom.lean) is now done, so this is unblocked.
      Note: f and [IsAddMonHom f] are section variables not mentioned in
      the statement, so they are currently NOT arguments of this def
      (needs `include f in` or explicit binders).
      The placeholder `blah` (l.268) should be removed or replaced.

